{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-04_vctr-ex99_1.htm, sha256 688618b95de22af1fbb40f51ed72f7946ede61600d66a4b0a7a7dc589f52e5c1.\nEX-99.1 2 vctr-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nNEWS RELEASE\nVictory Capital Reports Strong Third Quarter 2026 Results, Highlighted by Record Gross Sales and Net Flows\nThird Quarter Highlights\n\u2022 Record quarter-end total client assets of $355.5 billion \u2022 Record long-term gross sales of $30.5 billion \u2022 Record long-term net inflows of $11.7 billion \u2022 GAAP operating margin of 34.7% \u2022 GAAP net income per diluted share of $1.11 \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA margin of 53.5% \u2022 Adjusted net income with tax benefit per diluted share of $1.98 \u2022 Announced definitive agreement to acquire First Eagle Investments \u2022 Board declared regular quarterly cash dividend of $0.50 per share\nSan Antonio, Texas, November 4, 2026 \u2014 Victory Capital Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: VCTR) (\u201cVictory Capital\u201d or \u201cthe Company\u201d) today reported financial results for the quarter ended September 30, 2026.\n\u201cWe delivered record levels of both long-term gross sales of $30.5 billion and long-term net flows of $11.7 billion for the quarter, representing an annualized organic growth rate of approximately 14%,\u201d said David C. Brown, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer. \u201cYear to date, our long-term net flows reached $15.4 billion, and we achieved record quarter-end total client assets of $355.5 billion.\n\u201cThe drivers of our record gross sales and net flows were broad-based. Our U.S. intermediary, U.S. institutional and international channels each generated positive long-term net flows. Net flows were positive across numerous asset classes, including fixed income, solutions and global equity, with contributions from multiple Investment Franchises and our Solutions Platform, driven by our VictoryShares ETF platform. Together, these results showcase the breadth and depth of our product set and distribution, which allows us to align with client demand across market cycles.\n\u201cInvestment performance remained strong during the quarter. As of September 30, 2026, 60%, 69%, 63% and 77% of our AUM outperformed benchmarks over the respective 1-, 3-, 5- and 10-year periods. In addition, 62% of our rated mutual fund and ETF AUM had an Overall Morningstar Rating of four or five stars.\n\u201cWe continued to deliver an industry-leading margin. Our Adjusted EBITDA margin was 53.5% for the quarter and 54.0% year to date. Our margin reflects the durability of our platform and the discipline we apply across every dimension of our business.\n\u201cOur strong cash generation also supported meaningful capital return. During the quarter, we returned $81 million to shareholders, including $39 million to repurchase shares of VCTR common stock, with the balance paid as dividends.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "\u201cIn August 2026, we announced a definitive agreement to acquire First Eagle Investments. Acquiring First Eagle Investments is a transformational transaction that will add size and scale across our business and allow us to increase our distribution footprint inside and outside the United States. Additionally, it will add a differentiated global value multi-asset capability,\ncomplementary equity and fixed income capabilities, a scaled CLO and alternative credit platform, along with a track record of years of positive net flows, including year to date through the end of September 2026, as well as strong investment performance. Our teams are deeply engaged in integration planning and working toward closing. We expect the transaction to close by the end of the first quarter of 2027, subject to customary closing conditions, including certain regulatory approvals and client consents.\n\u201cAs always, we continue to focus on serving our clients, which is our top priority.\u201d\nDue to rounding, AUM values and other amounts in this press release may not add up precisely to the totals provided. The table below presents AUM, and certain GAAP and non-GAAP (\u201cadjusted\u201d) financial results.\n(in millions except per share amounts or as otherwise noted)\nFor the Three Months Ended\nFor the Nine Months Ended\nSeptember 30,\nJune 30,\nSeptember 30,\nSeptember 30,\nSeptember 30,\n2026\n2026\n2025\n2026\n2025\nAssets Under Management1\nEnding\n$\n351,869\n$\n342,450\n$\n310,644\n$\n351,869\n$\n310,644\nAverage\n350,630\n331,345\n303,584\n333,574\n254,117\nAUM Long-term Flows2\nLong-term Gross\n$\n30,488\n$\n22,113\n$\n16,962\n$\n71,548\n$\n41,694\nLong-term Net\n11,702\n4,201\n(244\n)\n15,446\n(2,109\n)\nAUM Money Market/Short-term Flows\nMoney Market / Short-term Gross\n$\n327\n$\n311\n$\n334\n$\n873\n$\n819\nMoney Market / Short-term Net\n(2\n)\n(91\n)\n(48\n)\n(290\n)\n(236\n)\nAUM Total Flows\nTotal Gross\n$\n30,816\n$\n22,424\n$\n17,296\n$\n72,