{"page": 3, "text": "2 Long-term AUM is defined as total AUM excluding Money Market and Short-term assets.\n3 The Company reports its financial results in accordance with GAAP. Adjusted EBITDA and Adjusted Net Income are not defined by GAAP and should not be regarded as an alternative to any measurement under GAAP. Please refer to the section \u201cInformation\n2\nRegarding Non-GAAP Financial Measures\u201d at the end of this press release for an explanation of Non-GAAP financial measures and a reconciliation to the nearest GAAP financial measure.\n4 The Company includes participating securities in its computation of adjusted earnings per diluted share, including shares of series A Non-Voting Convertible Preferred stock.\n3\nAUM, Flows and Investment Performance\nAt September 30, 2026, Victory Capital had total client assets of $355.5 billion, assets under management of $351.9 billion, and other assets of $3.6 billion. Total AUM increased by $9.4 billion to $351.9 billion at September 30, 2026, compared with $342.5 billion at June 30, 2026. The increase was primarily due to net inflows of $11.7 billion partially offset by negative market action of $2.2 billion.\nAs of September 30, 2026, Victory Capital offered 187 investment strategies through its multiple autonomous Investment Franchises and Solutions Platform. The table below presents outperformance against benchmarks by AUM as of September 30, 2026.\nPercentage of AUM Outperforming Benchmark\nTrailing\nTrailing\nTrailing\nTrailing\n1-Year\n3-Years\n5-Years\n10-Years\n60%\n69%\n63%\n77%\nThird Quarter 2026 Compared with Second Quarter 2026\nRevenue decreased 8.9% to $396.6 million in the third quarter, compared with $435.4 million in the second quarter, primarily due to the crystallization of certain annual fees received in the second quarter and changes in asset class and client mix, partially offset by higher average AUM over the comparable period. GAAP operating margin contracted by 980 basis points in the third quarter to 34.7%, down from 44.5% in the second quarter, due to a decrease in revenue and $16.2 million increase in acquisition-related costs as a result of the First Eagle Investments (\u201cFirst Eagle\u201d) transaction. Third quarter GAAP net income decreased 34.5% to $91.3 million, down from $139.4 million in the prior quarter.\nAdjusted net income with tax benefit decreased 10.7% to $163.2 million, or $1.98 per diluted share, in the third quarter, down from $182.9 million, or $2.21 per diluted share, in the second quarter. Adjusted EBITDA decreased $30.6 million to $212.1 million in the third quarter compared to $242.7 million in the second quarter. Adjusted EBITDA margin contracted 230 basis points in the third quarter of 2026 to 53.5% compared with 55.8% in the prior quarter.\nThird Quarter 2026 Compared with Third Quarter 2025\nRevenue for the three months ended September 30, 2026, increased 9.8% to $396.6 million, compared with $361.2 million in the same quarter of 2025 as a result of higher average AUM over the comparable period.\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "Operating expenses were $258.9 million compared with $223.1 million in last year\u2019s third quarter reflecting increases in variable operating expenses that rose as a result of higher average AUM and acquisition-related costs as a result of the First Eagle transaction, partially offset by a decrease in integration costs. GAAP operating margin contracted 350 basis points to 34.7% in the third quarter, from 38.2% in the same quarter of 2025. GAAP net income decreased 5.4% to $91.3 million in the third quarter compared with $96.5 million in the same quarter of 2025.\nAdjusted net income with tax benefit increased 15.5% to $163.2 million, or $1.98 per diluted share, in the third quarter, compared with $141.3 million, or $1.63 per diluted share in the same quarter last year. Adjusted EBITDA increased 11.4% to $212.1 million, compared with $190.5 million in the same quarter of last year. Year-over-year, adjusted EBITDA margin expanded 80 basis points to 53.5% in the third quarter of 2026, compared with 52.7% in the same quarter last year.\n4\nNine Months Ended September 30, 2026 Compared with Nine Months Ended September 30, 2025\nOn April 1, 2025, the Company completed the acquisition of Amundi US and reintroduced the brand Pioneer Investments for the acquired business and investment products. Year-over-year results reflect the acquisition of Amundi US, which closed on April 1, 2025. Revenue for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, increased 30.9% to $1.2 billion, compared with $932.0 million in the same period of 2025 as a result of higher average AUM over the comparable period.\nGAAP operating margin expanded 530 basis points to 40.2% in the nine months ended September 30, 2026, up from 34.9% in the same period of 2025. The improvement was due to decreases in acquisition-related and restructuring and integration costs of $12.4 million and $18.6 million, respectively, primarily related to the acquisition of Amundi US in 2025 partially offset by higher variable operating expenses as a result of the higher average AUM and an expanded business. Nine months ended September 30, 2026 GAAP net income increased 57.8% to $342.8 million, up from $217.3 million in the prior period.\nAdjusted net income with tax benefit increased 37.9% to $499.3 million, or $5.99 per diluted share, in the nine months ended September 30, 2026, compared with $362.2 million, or $4.59 per diluted share in the same period last year. Adjusted EBITDA increased 35.7% to $658.9 million, compared with $485.4 million in the same period of last year. Year-over-year, adjusted EBITDA margin expanded 190 basis points to 54.0% for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, compared with 52.1% in the same period of last year.\nBalance Sheet / Capital Management\nThe total debt outstanding as of September 30, 2026 was approximately $975 million.\nFor the three months ended September 30, 2026, the Company repurchased approximately 0.4 million shares of Common Stock.\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "The Company\u2019s Board of Directors approved a regular quarterly cash dividend of $0.50 per share. The dividend is payable on December 23, 2026, to shareholders of record on December 10, 2026.\nConference Call, Webcast and Slide Presentation\nThe Company will host a conference call tomorrow morning, November 5, at 8:00 a.m. ET to discuss the results. Analysts and investors may participate in the question-and-answer session. To participate in the conference call, please call 1-833-461-5787 (domestic) or 1-585-542-9983 (international), shortly before 8:00 a.m. ET and reference the Meeting ID 160 367 883. A live, listen-only webcast will also be available via the investor relations section of the Company\u2019s website at https://ir.vcm.com. Prior to the call, a supplemental slide presentation that will be used during the conference call will be available on the Events and Presentations page of the Company\u2019s investor relations website. For anyone who is unable to join the live event, an archive of the webcast will be available for replay shortly after the call concludes.\nAbout Victory Capital\nVictory Capital (NASDAQ: VCTR) is a diversified global asset management firm with $355.5 billion in total client assets, as of September 30, 2026. We serve institutional, intermediary, and individual clients through our Investment Franchises and Solutions Platform, which manage\n5\nspecialized investment strategies across traditional and alternative asset classes. Our differentiated approach combines the power of investment autonomy with the support of a robust, fully integrated operational and distribution platform. Clients have access to focused, top-tier investment talent equipped with comprehensive resources designed to deliver competitive long-term performance.\nVictory Capital is headquartered in San Antonio, Texas. To learn more, visit www.vcm.com or follow us on Facebook, Twitter (X), and LinkedIn.\nFORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n"}
