 procedures and capabilities; the Company's substantial indebtedness; the potential impairment of the Company\u2019s goodwill and intangible assets; disruption to the operations of third parties whose functions are integral to the Company\u2019s ETF platform; the Company's determination that we are not required to register as an \u201cinvestment company\u201d under the Investment Company Act of 1940; the fluctuation of the Company\u2019s expenses; the Company's ability to respond to recent trends in the investment management industry; the level of regulation on investment management firms and the Company\u2019s ability to\n6\nrespond to regulatory developments; the competitiveness of the investment management industry; and other risks and factors included, but not limited to, those listed under the caption \u201cRisk Factors\u201d in Item 1A of the Company\u2019s Annual Report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2025, filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (the \u201cSEC\u201d) on February 26, 2026, which is accessible on the SEC\u2019s website at www.sec.gov.\n"}
{"page": 8, "text": "In light of these risks, uncertainties and other factors, the forward-looking statements contained in this press release might not prove to be accurate. All forward-looking statements speak only as of the date made and Victory Capital undertakes no obligation to update or revise publicly any forward-looking statements, whether as a result of new information, future events or otherwise.\nInvestment Performance and Fund Ratings\nWe believe that investment performance can influence AUM growth, flows, and overall operational results. Management utilizes the percentage of AUM and the percentage of strategies outperforming benchmarks, together with the percentage of our rated mutual fund and ETF AUM and the number of our mutual funds and ETFs rated 4 or 5 stars overall by Morningstar, to evaluate the investment performance of our Investment Franchises, our Solutions Platform, and specific investment products.\nAUM measured versus benchmark on a one, three, five, and 10-year basis represents 90%, 89%, 85%, and 78% of Total AUM, respectively, as of September 30, 2026. Composites are calculated by asset weighting included accounts, using gross-of-fee, linked time weighted returns for each period. The composite return is then compared to the primary strategy benchmark. Composites without sufficient performance history are excluded from periods for which a full track record does not yet exist. Certain separate accounts are excluded where Victory Capital has determined, in accordance with its GIPS\u00ae Procedures, that inclusion would not be representative of the strategy's performance.\nAs of September 30, 2026, of our 113 rated mutual funds and ETFs, 56 received 4 or 5 star Overall Morningstar RatingsTM, and 57 did not, representing 62% and 38% of rated mutual fund and ETF AUM, respectively. Funds not rated by Morningstar are excluded from the analysis. Not all asset classes considered are available to the general public and not all funds included have a history to be included in each period. Had fees not been waived and/or expenses reimbursed currently or in the past, the Morningstar ratings could have been lower. Ratings for other share classes not shown may be lower.\nPast performance is not indicative of future results and may not reflect an investor's experience.\nContacts\nInvestors:\nCarly Thomas\nDirector, Investor Relations and Responsible Business\n210-694-9658\ncthomas@vcm.com\nMedia:\nJessica Davila Burgess\nDirector, Global Communications\n210-694-9693\njessica_davila@vcm.com\n7\nVictory Capital Holdings, Inc. and Subsidiaries\nUnaudited Consolidated Statements of Operations\n(in thousands except per share data and percentages)\nFor the Three Months Ended\nFor the Nine Months Ended\nSeptember 30,\nJune 30,\nSeptember 30,\nSeptember 30,\nSeptember 30,\n2026\n2026\n2025\n2026\n2025\nRevenue\nInvestment management fees\n$\n322,085\n$\n362,243\n$\n288,509\n$\n1,000,697\n$\n744,116\nFund administration and distribution fees\n74,488\n73,118\n72,686\n219,226\n187,893\nTotal revenue\n396,573\n435,361\n"}
